{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Gradient Checkpointing and Activation Recomputation Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: A Toy Model With Segments"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import numpy as np"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def linear_forward(x, w, b):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return x @ w + b"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def relu(x):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return np.maximum(x, 0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def layer_forward(x, w1, b1, w2, b2):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    h = relu(linear_forward(x, w1, b1))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return linear_forward(h, w2, b2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def model_forward(x, params):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    activations = [x]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    h = x"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for w1, b1, w2, b2 in params:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        h = layer_forward(h, w1, b1, w2, b2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        activations.append(h)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return h, activations"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: Naive Backward Needing All Activations"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def model_backward(grad_output, activations, params):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    grads = [None] * len(params)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    g = grad_output"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for i in range(len(params) - 1, -1, -1):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        w1, b1, w2, b2 = params[i]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x_in = activations[i]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        h_pre = linear_forward(x_in, w1, b1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        h = relu(h_pre)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        gh = g @ w2.T"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        gw2 = h.T @ g"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        gb2 = g.sum(axis=0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        g_pre = gh * (h_pre > 0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        gx = g_pre @ w1.T"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        gw1 = x_in.T @ g_pre"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        gb1 = g_pre.sum(axis=0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        grads[i] = (gw1, gb1, gw2, gb2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        g = gx"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return g, grads"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: Checkpoint-Every-k Memory"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def model_forward_checkpointed(x, params, k=4):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    saved_inputs = [x]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    h = x"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for i, (w1, b1, w2, b2) in enumerate(params):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        h = layer_forward(h, w1, b1, w2, b2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if (i + 1) % k == 0:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            saved_inputs.append(h)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return h, saved_inputs"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def model_backward_checkpointed(grad_output, saved_inputs, params, k=4):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    grads = [None] * len(params)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    g = grad_output"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    segments = [(j * k, min((j + 1) * k, len(params))) for j in range(len(saved_inputs))]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for seg_idx in range(len(saved_inputs) - 1, -1, -1):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        start, end = segments[seg_idx]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if start >= end:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            continue"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x_in = saved_inputs[seg_idx]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        _, seg_acts = model_forward(x_in, params[start:end])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        g, seg_grads = model_backward(g, seg_acts, params[start:end])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for j, gr in enumerate(seg_grads):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            grads[start + j] = gr"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return g, grads"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: Cost Model"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def checkpoint_cost(n_layers, segment_size, flops_per_layer=1.0):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    fwd = n_layers * flops_per_layer"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    recompute = n_layers * flops_per_layer"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    bwd = 2 * n_layers * flops_per_layer"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return {"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"fwd\": fwd,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"recompute\": recompute,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"bwd\": bwd,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"total\": fwd + recompute + bwd,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"overhead_vs_no_ckpt\": (fwd + recompute + bwd) / (fwd + bwd) - 1.0,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    }"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def selective_checkpoint_cost(n_layers, attention_fraction=0.15,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                              flops_per_layer=1.0):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    fwd = n_layers * flops_per_layer"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    recompute = n_layers * attention_fraction * flops_per_layer"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    bwd = 2 * n_layers * flops_per_layer"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return {"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"fwd\": fwd,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"recompute\": recompute,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"bwd\": bwd,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"total\": fwd + recompute + bwd,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"overhead_vs_no_ckpt\": (fwd + recompute + bwd) / (fwd + bwd) - 1.0,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    }"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 5: Memory Estimator"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def activation_memory_mb(n_layers, hidden=8192, seq=8192,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                        batch=1, bytes_per_value=2):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    per_layer = 12 * batch * seq * hidden * bytes_per_value"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return n_layers * per_layer / 1e6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def memory_after_checkpoint(n_layers, segment_size, hidden=8192,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                           seq=8192, batch=1, bytes_per_value=2):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    n_seg = max(1, n_layers // segment_size)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    saved = (n_seg + segment_size) * 1 * batch * seq * hidden * bytes_per_value"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return saved / 1e6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 6: Optimal Segment Size"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def optimal_segment(n_layers):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return int(round(np.sqrt(n_layers)))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 7: Selective Checkpoint Decision"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def should_recompute(layer_type, activation_bytes, recompute_flops_ratio):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if layer_type == \"attention\" and activation_bytes > 100 * 1e6:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return True"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if layer_type == \"ffn\" and activation_bytes > 500 * 1e6:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return recompute_flops_ratio < 0.1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return False"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. Verify correctness. Run `model_forward` + `model_backward` (full activations) vs `model_forward_checkpointed` + `model_backward_checkpointed` (segments). Parameter gradients must be identical to machine precision.\n\n2. Sweep segment size `k` from 1 to `L`. Plot FLOP overhead and memory. Find the knee of the curve.\n\n3. Implement selective checkpointing: store the attention-module input but not its intermediates. Measure the FLOP overhead vs full-layer checkpointing for a 32-layer model at seq=8192.\n\n4. Add offload. Save segment inputs to a simulated \"CPU buffer\" (a separate list). Measure \"PCIe bandwidth\" as bytes/time and find the breakeven point between offload and recompute.\n\n5. Benchmark a real PyTorch transformer with and without `torch.utils.checkpoint`. Measure memory (via `torch.cuda.max_memory_allocated`) and step time."
      ]
    }
